================================================================================================================
STRUCTURAL CORRECTNESS -- bug-catchers, not judgment calls
================================================================================================================
  The target is a running max in k, and quantiles are ordered in q. Both are
  HARD constraints, so both are now ENFORCED rather than gated on.

  THIS WAS A GATE AND THE GATE WAS WRONG. It required zero violations, and
  it counted them across all five horizons at once, so a single violation
  anywhere disqualified every horizon of that model. Each horizon is an
  INDEPENDENT fit -- nothing forces the 10h fit above the 5h fit on a given
  episode -- so cross-horizon violations are normal behaviour, not a bug.
  Measured on val: QTREE/MAE had 7,060 monotonicity violations of 385,060
  (1.833%) and 8 quantile crossings (0.002%). Climatology cannot violate
  either. The rule therefore failed every conditional model BY CONSTRUCTION
  and would have retired the feature set on an artifact.

  populationdir  model         quantile enforce    horizon enforce
  ALL       MAE  Climatology             0.000%             0.000%
  ALL       MAE  Linear QR               0.000%             0.002%
  ALL       MAE  QTREE                   0.000%             0.624%
  ALL       MAE  kNN                     0.000%             0.000%
  ALL       MFE  Climatology             0.000%             0.000%
  ALL       MFE  Linear QR               0.000%             0.002%
  ALL       MFE  QTREE                   0.000%             0.372%
  ALL       MFE  kNN                     0.000%             0.000%
  TRENDING  MAE  Climatology             0.000%             0.000%
  TRENDING  MAE  Linear QR               0.000%             0.004%
  TRENDING  MAE  QTREE                   0.000%             0.664%
  TRENDING  MAE  kNN                     0.000%             0.000%
  TRENDING  MFE  Climatology             0.000%             0.000%
  TRENDING  MFE  Linear QR               0.000%             0.000%
  TRENDING  MFE  QTREE                   0.000%             0.443%
  TRENDING  MFE  kNN                     0.000%             0.000%
  Rates are the share of (episode, horizon, quantile) predictions that
  enforcement MOVED. 0.000% means the model already satisfied the
  constraint. Climatology and kNN cannot violate either: np.quantile is
  non-decreasing in q, and the quantile of a running maximum is
  non-decreasing in k. Independent per-horizon fits have no such guarantee.

================================================================================================================
CALIBRATION -- this decides which models get their sharpness compared
================================================================================================================
  A coverage number is CONSISTENT if its day-clustered 95% interval contains
  the quantile it targets. Slices: predicted-magnitude decile, realized-
  magnitude decile, and early/late half of the held-out period.
  Admissible = all 5 aggregate quantiles consistent AND inconsistent slices
  no more than 2x the 5% expected by chance. The monotonicity and
  crossing constraints are ENFORCED above and are NOT part of this rule.

  CELL COUNT: 2 populations x 2 directions x 4 models x 5 horizons = 80 cells.
  Each prints a PASS/fail and, below, a ratio against climatology. BOTH
  WILL BE READ AS FINDINGS whatever this run calls itself, so the chance
  rates are stated here rather than left to be worked out later.
  The aggregate screen is 5 interval checks at 95%, so a PERFECTLY
  calibrated cell clears it only 77.4% of the time: about
  18 of 80 cells would fail on chance alone.
  This screen's error runs toward FALSE FAILURE, not false discovery.
  On the slice side, 5% of slices are expected inconsistent by chance and
  the tolerance is 2x that.

